================================================================================
Virtual attributes — UC-function-computed attributes, resolved on demand
================================================================================

Context: every attribute an ontology could carry had to be fed by a mapping and
materialized by a build, so a value that is a *function of* the entity rather
than a fact stored about it (a live risk score, a current inventory position, a
distance to the nearest hub) had nowhere to live. The workaround was a class
action, which is a verb the user clicks — wrong affordance for something that
reads as an attribute, and invisible to an agent asking "what do you know about
this customer". Virtual attributes fill that gap: declared on the class like any
other attribute, computed by a Unity Catalog function from the entity's ID at
the moment someone asks, never materialized. The trade is stated everywhere it
matters — they are not queryable in SPARQL, GraphQL or a cohort, and take no
part in mappings, R2RML, SHACL or data-quality checks.

The declarations live in a new `cls["virtualAttributes"]` list rather than in
`dataProperties`, which is what keeps them out of every downstream pipeline
without a single guard clause in those pipelines. No registry migration: the
ontology is already a `jsonb` blob.

Falls under the AI feature lifecycle gate (`.cursor/12`): the MCP tool contract
changes, so SPEC.md and an eval dataset ship with the change.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/databricks/uc/UnityCatalog.py`
   `list_functions` now returns `return_type` and `return_columns` (the
   `RETURNS TABLE` result columns in declaration order). Read by a *second*
   statement on `information_schema.parameters` filtered to the complement of
   the `IN` predicate: aggregating input parameters and result columns in one
   join multiplies rows. A metastore that cannot answer the second query logs a
   warning and yields empty `return_columns` rather than losing the function
   list, which the Actions picker also depends on.
2. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/VirtualAttributeService.py` (new)
   Declaration reading (`class_entries`) and computation (`compute`). Reading is
   forgiving by contract: a group with an unsafe `fullName`, an unusable column
   or a duplicate attribute name is logged and skipped, because one bad
   declaration must not cost the node its whole context. Computation isolates
   per group — a failing UC function carries an `error` and leaves the other
   groups' values intact. Only the first row is used (a virtual attribute is
   single-valued per entity, so several rows is a declaration error, reported
   via `message` rather than aggregated), and a scalar function is read through
   the reserved `result` alias.
3. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/NodeContextService.py`
   `resolve_context` gained `compute_virtual_attributes`; declarations always
   ride along with the class lookup, values only on request. Added the
   `compute_virtual_attributes` facade for callers that want the values without
   a fresh dataset/bridge resolution — the Graph Explorer's Compute button. The
   policy check precedes the class lookup, so a disabled element does not leak
   whether the URI resolves.
4. `src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py`, `src/back/core/helpers/__init__.py`
   Promoted the `_SAFE_SQL_IDENT` / `_SAFE_COL_IDENT` regexes out of
   `NodeContextService` into module-level `SAFE_SQL_IDENT` / `SAFE_COL_IDENT`.
   The new service needs the same guards, and importing them from
   `NodeContextService` would have inverted the dependency.
5. `src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py`
   `build_class_from_data` carries `virtualAttributes`, falling back to the
   existing value so a save from a panel that does not know about them cannot
   wipe the declarations.
6. `src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py`,
   `src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyParser.py`
   Round-trip through an `ONTOBRICKS_NS.virtualAttributes` JSON literal, kept
   deliberately out of the `owl:DatatypeProperty` block. A malformed literal is
   swallowed: an unreadable declaration must not make the ontology unloadable.
7. `src/back/core/mcp_tools.py`
   New `virtual_attributes` context element, so a domain can push it
   (*preferred*) or take it off the table (*disabled*).
8. `src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py`
   `NodeContextVirtualAttribute` / `NodeContextVirtualAttributeGroup` response
   models and the `compute_virtual_attributes` query flag on
   `GET /nodes/context`. `values` is omitted rather than emptied when nothing
   was computed: the difference between *not computed* and *computed as null*
   is load-bearing for an agent.
9. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   `GET /dtwin/classes` exposes the declarations, `/dtwin/nodes/context` takes
   the flag, and a new `GET /dtwin/nodes/virtual-attributes` computes on demand
   with an optional `function` filter — the Graph Explorer's per-group button.
10. `src/api/routers/domains.py`
    `/domain/classes` publishes `virtualAttributes` through
    `VirtualAttributeService.class_entries`, so the MCP server caches normalized
    declarations rather than raw ontology JSON.
11. `src/mcp-server/server/app.py`
    `get_entity_context` gained `compute_virtual_attributes` and refuses it when
    the element is disabled, rather than answering with nothing — same contract
    as the actions overlap. `describe_entity` names the declarations with a
    count; the node-context formatter renders `not computed` placeholders and
    swaps the "call with the flag" hint for the values once they arrive, so the
    model is never asked to redo work it just did.
12. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js`
    Virtual Attributes box in the **Attributes** tab, with its own UC function
    picker. Factored the catalog → schema → function cascade out of the Actions
    picker (`_ucFillCatalogSelect`, `_ucFillSchemaSelect`, `_ucFetchFunctions`,
    `_ucClosePickerModal`) instead of copying it. Picking a function derives one
    attribute per returned column, deduplicated against the class's mapped *and*
    virtual names (`score` → `score_2`) since the Explorer and MCP render both
    families in one list. Removal is per function group: the attributes are the
    function's signature, so dropping one alone would leave the
    column-to-attribute mapping ambiguous.
13. `src/front/static/query/js/query-virtual-attributes.js` (new)
    The Explorer's section renderer and compute client. Values are cached per
    entity *and* function for the page's lifetime, so revisiting a node costs
    nothing and the button reads `Recompute`. Results are matched back to their
    DOM block by function name, not by position — a single-group computation
    returns one entry, which would otherwise land on the first group's rows.
14. `src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js`,
    `src/front/static/query/js/query-entity-details.js`,
    `src/front/static/query/js/query-loaders.js`,
    `src/front/templates/dtwin.html`
    Section under Attributes in both detail renderers, plus a **Compute virtual
