================================================================================
Fix: a pending detail-panel edit was lost when leaving the page
================================================================================

Context
-------
Reported against the new virtual attributes, but not specific to them: removing
a virtual attribute and then clicking straight on the Knowledge Graph menu lost
the change. The entity detail panel is an edit buffer, and it was already
flushed on every exit but one:

- closing it via the X       -> `guardedCloseSharedPanel` saves first
- switching sidebar section  -> `checkDirtyBeforeSwitch` saves first
- opening another item       -> `checkDirtyBeforeSwitch` saves first
- leaving for another route  -> nothing

Knowledge Graph, Mapping and Domain are separate routes, so the click was a
full page navigation and none of the in-page hooks ran. Worse, the page already
auto-saves on unload: `saveRegistryOnUnload` then persisted a session that had
never heard about the pending edit, which is what made the loss durable instead
of merely transient. Any panel field was affected — a removed action, a renamed
entity — the virtual attribute was just the one that surfaced it.

Changes
-------
1. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js` — added
   `flushSharedPanelOnUnload`, registered on `beforeunload` and `pagehide`.
   It is deliberately not awaited: only the synchronous prefix of the save can
   run before teardown, and that prefix is the part that matters — it commits
   the edit to `OntologyState.config` and dispatches the session save. The tail
   (constraints, OWL regeneration, notifications) is skipped; the OWL is
   regenerated from the config on the next load. The flush is a no-op on a
   clean or read-only panel, so it is safe to call twice.
2. `src/front/static/global/js/ontology-core.js` — `saveConfigToSession` takes
   an optional `keepalive` flag. Without it the browser cancels the request
   during page teardown, which is the mechanism by which the edit vanished.
   `saveSharedEntity` and `saveSharedRelationship` forward the flag.
3. `src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js` — `saveRegistryOnUnload`
   calls the flush first. This is an ordering fix, not a duplicate: the panel
   module is loaded after the design module, so its own unload listener runs
   second and the registry would still be written from the stale session. Same
   dependency the layout beacon already documents.
4. `tests/units/front/test_shared_panel_unload_flush.py` (new) — five guards:
   the handlers are registered, the flush no-ops when there is nothing to save,
   the session save is keepalive on that path, the flush precedes the registry
   save inside `saveRegistryOnUnload` (scoped to that function, since
   `autoSaveToRegistry` shares the `registryDirty` guard), and the pre-existing
   exits still flush.

