## Explorer-parity split panel for Ontology Designer / Entities / Relationships

Context: the three ontology sections shared a right-hand detail panel built as
a drawer — `width: 0` until a `.panel-open` class widened it to 380px, injected
*inside* the canvas container, with an 11px handle painted in Bootstrap blue
(`#0d6efd`). The Knowledge Graph Explorer next door already had the layout we
want: canvas and panel as two framed cards side by side, 0.5rem gutter, slim
drag handle, panel permanently visible with a placeholder. Aligned the three
ontology sections on it, then adjusted the tab frame and the canvas selection
colour.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-shared-panels.css`
   Panel is permanent: `420px` default (fits the 4-tab form strip on one
   line), `min-width: 200px`, `max-width: 50%`; dropped the `width: 0` +
   `.panel-open` drawer. Handle rebuilt as the Explorer's 8px hit area with a
   3px x 40px bar, `--db-border` at rest and `--db-primary` on hover/drag.
   Added `ob-split-shell` (frameless wrapper) and `ob-split-pane` (framed
   content side) so both panes carry the same border and radius as the panel.
   Added the `.panel-placeholder` empty state; removed the close-button rules.

2. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js`
   `ensureDetailPanels()` creates the panel on DOMContentLoaded — D3 sizes the
   canvas from `container.clientWidth` once, so a panel appearing later left
   the graph centred on the wrong axis. Panel now hosted on
   `ontology-map-wrapper` instead of `ontology-map-container`, making it a
   sibling of the canvas so the canvas can be framed as a pane. Closing
   renders the placeholder instead of collapsing; resize clamps to 200-900px.
   Removed the close button and `setupPanelListeners`.

3. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js`
   Clicking the empty canvas clears the panel via `guardedCloseSharedPanel`,
   which is now the only exit and so must flush a pending edit. Connection
   line stroke moved off Bootstrap blue.

4. `src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-map.css`
   Entity / relationship selection, neighbour rings, highlighted links and
   labels, hitarea dots and connection-source states use `--db-primary` /
   `--db-primary-rgb` instead of `#0d6efd`. The selected node itself was grey;
