## Button design audit — focus regression, responsive headers and two design islands

Context: a systematic audit of every button across the 59 sections (desktop and
mobile) found that resting states were sound almost everywhere, but that focus
was globally broken, small joined controls had drifted off the radius token,
section headers could not wrap, and two surfaces had grown their own button
languages. This pass fixes all of it.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/global/css/components.css`
   Fixed the global focus regression: Bootstrap's `:focus-visible` repaints a
   button with its *hover* palette, which for the unfilled variants is the solid
   Bootstrap fill the design drops — so focusing an outline button turned it
   solid grey, blue or red. Both `:focus` and `:focus-visible` now pin the
   resting background, border and text for every neutral and outline variant,
   leaving `--db-focus-ring` to carry the state. `.btn-outline-danger` keeps its
   red lettering through a follow-up rule.

2. `src/front/static/global/css/main.css`
   - `.section-header` and any flex cluster inside it now wrap, and below 768px
     a `.btn-group` in a header becomes individually rounded `nowrap` pills.
     `justify-content-between` does not wrap, so the control cluster used to
     push its last buttons off-screen while the survivors stretched to three
     times their height.
   - Re-pinned Bootstrap's `-sm` size ramp to `--db-radius-control`
     (`.form-control-sm`, `.form-select-sm`, `.input-group-sm > *`). Bootstrap
     sets `border-radius` there as a property with enough specificity to beat
     the base rule, so small joined controls silently used its legacy 4px.

3. `src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_map.html`,
   `src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-assistant.css`
   Removed the ontology assistant FAB — a 56px circular button in hard-coded
   Databricks orange with its own shadows and inline SVG, floating over the
   canvas against the section-header rule. The assistant now opens from a
   regular icon button in the header. The popup keeps its bottom-right anchor,
   moved down to where the FAB used to sit.

4. `src/front/static/query/css/query-chat.css`
   Removed the Graph Chat design island: every `#FF3621` orange, `#64748b` cold
   grey and `#B91C1C` red is now a Clarity token, the header action defers to
   the global button contract instead of redefining pill radii and an orange
   hover, the input wrapper uses `--db-focus-ring`, and the pending-action
   buttons use the control radius.

5. Section header toolbars grouped and CTA hierarchy fixed, per the documented
   order (icon utilities -> secondary CTAs -> primary CTA rightmost):
   - `partials/ontology/_ontology_map.html`,
     `partials/mapping/_mapping_design.html`: loose icon buttons separated by
     `.vr` rules are now `.btn-group.btn-group-sm` clusters, with `aria-label`
     on each. The two buttons that `permissions.css` *hides* for viewers stay
     out of the groups: a hidden member would leave its neighbour squared.
   - `partials/ontology/_ontology_design.html`: grouped the two loose
     utilities, dropped the `|` text separators.
   - Promoted the section CTA to `btn-primary` and moved the discussion
     shortcut ahead of it in `_ontology_entities.html`,
     `_ontology_relationships.html`, `_ontology_wizard.html`,
     `_domain_metadata.html`, `_mapping_autoassign.html`,
     `_mapping_diagnostics.html`, `_pitfalls.html`, `_ontology_cohorts.html`,
     `_query_cohorts.html` (Materialise is the terminal action, Preview a step)
     and `_query_sync.html`.
   - `static/query/js/query-sync.js`: the "Go to Build" shortcut inside the
     status badge is no longer `btn-primary` — it is a navigation hint, not the
     section CTA.
   - Normalised misleading `btn-outline-warning` / `-success` to
     `-secondary`, which is what the design renders them as anyway.

6. `src/front/templates/settings.html`
   Added the missing `btn-sm` to the four `.btn-save-settings` and to
   `#btnOpenProvisionModal`; without it they were 110px tall on a phone.

7. Initial visibility moved from inline styles to `d-none`, with the JS
   toggling the class: `#btnInitRegistry`, `#btnImportObxConfirm`,
   `#graphqlOpenNewTab`, `#brSuggestAcceptBtn`, `#dqSuggestAcceptBtn`
   (the last two were found by the new test, not the audit). The two
   suggestion-accept buttons also gained `btn-sm` and moved from
   `btn-success` to `btn-primary`.

8. `.cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc`
   Documented the button state contract, the responsive header behaviour, the
   `-sm` radius pinning, and three new anti-patterns (utility after the CTA,
   inline `display:none`, permission-hidden button inside a group).

9. `tests/units/front/test_button_design_contract.py`
   New file, 19 tests: unfilled variants stay unfilled when focused (per
   variant), danger keeps its red text, small joined controls use the token,
   headers wrap, grouped buttons become pills when wrapping, no FAB exists,
   permission-hidden buttons stay out of groups, the chat uses tokens, settings
   headers carry `btn-sm`, no button is hidden with an inline style, and the
   primary CTA is the rightmost button in ten section headers.

